    <article>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="meta">Natural Phonics Cat · Effective 8 October 2026</p>

      <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how Natural Phonics Cat (&quot;we&quot;,
        &quot;us&quot;, &quot;our&quot;) handles information when you use our
        Android application and any related website or progressive web app
        (together, the &quot;Service&quot;). We design the Service for phonics
        learning. We do not require you to create an account.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy or your data:
        <a href="mailto:llathk001@gmail.com">llathk001@gmail.com</a>
      </p>

      <h2>3. Summary</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Android app (Google Play):</strong> Learning progress is stored
          on your device only. We do not run third-party analytics inside the
          native app. Audio and images are bundled in the app or played locally.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Website / PWA (if you use our site in a browser):</strong> In
          production we may use Vercel Analytics and Speed Insights (usage and
          performance metrics). A service worker may cache content for offline
          use.
        </li>
        <li><strong>We do not sell</strong> your personal information.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Information stored on your device</h2>
      <p>
        The Service saves practice data in your browser or app WebView storage
        (for example <code>localStorage</code>), including:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Spaced-repetition progress for phonics items (non-personal identifiers
          such as grapheme and phoneme keys)
        </li>
        <li>A list of items you missed for review in the game</li>
        <li>
          Game setup choices during your session (for example selected practice
          scope)
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This data stays on your device unless you clear app or browser storage,
        uninstall the app, or reset your device. We do not receive this data on
        our servers because we do not operate a login or cloud sync for progress
        at this time.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Information we do not collect</h2>
      <p>Through the app as currently built, we do not ask for or collect:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Name, email, or phone number inside the app</li>
        <li>Precise location</li>
        <li>Contacts, photos, or files on your device</li>
        <li>
          Advertising identifiers for in-app ads (the app does not show
          third-party ads)
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. Device features and third parties</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Text-to-speech:</strong> Example words (for example on posters or
        picture mode) may be read aloud using your device&apos;s system
        text-to-speech engine. The word text is processed on your device by the
        operating system or platform provider (such as Google on Android), not
        sent to us.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Audio:</strong> Phoneme sounds may play from files included in the
        app or site.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Internet:</strong> The Android app is designed to work largely
        offline after install. A network permission may be used for future
        features (such as subscription verification). When you use the public
        website, standard web hosting and CDN providers process requests to
        deliver pages and assets.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Google Play:</strong> If you purchase a subscription or in-app
        product in the future, payment and purchase records are handled by Google
        Play under Google&apos;s privacy policy. We may receive subscription
        status through Google Play or a billing partner (such as RevenueCat) to
        unlock features, not your full payment card details.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Vercel (website only):</strong> If you visit our production
        website, Vercel may process analytics and performance data as described in
        <a
          href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank"
          >Vercel&apos;s Privacy Policy</a
        >. This does not apply inside the native Android app build.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Children&apos;s privacy</h2>
      <p>
        The Service is intended for learners, including children, under the
        supervision of a parent, guardian, or educator. We do not knowingly
        collect personal information from children online. Practice data remains
        on the device. If you believe a child has provided personal information
        to us by email, contact us and we will delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Retention and security</h2>
      <p>
        On-device data remains until you remove it or uninstall the app. We use
        reasonable measures to protect any information we handle, but no method
        of transmission or storage is completely secure.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Your choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Clear site data or app storage to reset progress</li>
        <li>Uninstall the Android app</li>
        <li>
          Disable or limit analytics in your browser when using the website
          (browser settings or extensions)
        </li>
        <li>
          Contact us to ask questions or request deletion of information you sent
          us by email
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>10. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy. We will post the new version on this
        page and update the effective date. Continued use of the Service after
        changes means you accept the updated policy.
      </p>

      <hr />

